    {
      "v": 5,
      "zh": "大卫说：「我儿子所罗门还年幼娇嫩，要为耶和华建造的殿宇必须高大辉煌，使名誉荣耀传遍万国；所以我要为殿预备材料。」于是，大卫在未死之先预备的材料甚多。",
      "en": "David said, “My son Solomon is just an inexperienced young man,[NOTE:1] and the temple to be built for the Lord must be especially magnificent so it will become famous and be considered splendid by all the nations.[NOTE:2] Therefore I will make preparations for its construction.” So David made extensive preparations before he died.",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “a young man and tender.”",
        "Heb “and the house to build to make exceedingly great for a name and for splendor for all the lands.”"
